From 482e6ac4a04a0d5aca57e5a5f6e40417dc546f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:17:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] os/kernel/paging: Add ASSERT hitting test case for
 pg_miss

pg_miss() blocks the faulting task and then signals the page fill worker
thread to resolve the fault. If the faulting task were the worker itself
nothing could ever service the fill, so pg_miss() guards against it with
DEBUGASSERT(g_pgworker != ftcb->pid).

Add a negative test case which points g_pgworker at the calling task and
then calls pg_miss(), which is exactly the state the assertion defends
against. g_pgworker is restored on the path taken when the assertion is
compiled out.

 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_paging.c : kernel side
   helper reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_PAGING ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_paging.c : user side
   test case. A return from the ioctl is reported as a test case failure.

Controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_PAGING, default n, depends on
CONFIG_PAGING and CONFIG_DEBUG. It crashes the board by design and must
be enabled alone.
